# std/edit — one of the file tools (std/files holds the source they share).
# The help is a HERE-STRING so it lives in this expression, which is stripped
# from the tree the build sees: editing the docs re-keys this tool's ArgTree and
# nothing it builds from.
HELP=<<END
Replace text in a file. `root` is the file, such as sources/repo/99-dirty/README.md. `old-string` must match the file content exactly and (unless `replace-all`) appear exactly once: include surrounding context to disambiguate. Prefer this over sed via bash. Editing inside a source tree makes a child commit of it.
@param old-string Exact text to replace.
@param new-string Replacement text.
@param [replace-all] Replace every occurrence (default false).
@writer
@root
END
IMAGE=run --base:@=DEEP-DEPS/rustc --src:@=DEEP-DEPS/files
curry --base=$IMAGE --op=edit --help=$HELP
